{id:"BG003",kind:"mathematical",at:"/inference/argument/2/text",fact:"For inverse K-linear maps s:U→T and t:T→U, if s a=A s for endomorphisms a of U and A of T, then s sends any a-invariant K-subspace W of U to an A-invariant K-subspace s(W) of T. If s(W) is invariant under B∈End_K(T), then W is invariant under tBs.",grounds:[{location:"/inference/argument/0/produces/0",reason:"F001 gives inverse K-linear maps and intertwinings for every induced lattice operator, in particular x and y."},{location:"/inference/argument/1/produces/0",reason:"F002 applies to every x̂,ŷ-invariant K-subspace of T."},{location:"/inference/argument/2/text",reason:"W is an arbitrary K-subspace invariant under the original induced x,y; G_ij is defined as tF_ij s."}],justification:"The image of a subspace under a linear map is a subspace. For w∈W, A(s(w))=s(a(w)) lies in s(W). If B(s(w))∈s(W), write it as s(w') with w'∈W; then tBs(w)=ts(w')=w'∈W. Apply this with the two intertwined generators and then each F_ij."}
